{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-2355" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The displacement (in meters) of a particle moving in a straight line is given by the equation $s(t)={t}^{3}-{t}^{2}-15$ where $t$ is measured in seconds.  Find the velocity after $t=3\\,\\text{s}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033872/state.json" "file_sha256" "6884fe35829bc5bfacf0148ddddb8ee441b842cbc9f885bcf5b9b0c932c1d8c8"} {"question" "q-2355" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we calculate the velocity function by differentiating the position function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}s}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{3}-{t}^{2}-15) \\\\  & =3{t}^{2}-2t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo calculate the velocity at $t=3\\,\\text{s},$ we substitute $t=3$ into the velocity function above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(3) & =3(3)^{2}-2(3) \\\\  & =27-6 \\\\  & =21\\,\\text{m/s}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033872/state.json" "file_sha256" "6884fe35829bc5bfacf0148ddddb8ee441b842cbc9f885bcf5b9b0c932c1d8c8"} {"question" "q-2355" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033872/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b47cbfa9e32ceac06bca1e70e5aba7e83a133b3e6bc5cebf3ecfee8b04c7ad85"} {"question" "q-2355" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033872/state.json" "file_sha256" "6884fe35829bc5bfacf0148ddddb8ee441b842cbc9f885bcf5b9b0c932c1d8c8"} {"question" "q-2355" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "14\\,\\text{m/s}"] ["math" "19\\,\\text{m/s}"] ["math" "21\\,\\text{m/s}"] ["math" "27\\,\\text{m/s}"] ["math" "3\\,\\text{m/s}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033872/state.json" "file_sha256" "6884fe35829bc5bfacf0148ddddb8ee441b842cbc9f885bcf5b9b0c932c1d8c8"} {"question" "q-2355" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "21\\,\\text{m/s}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033872/state.json" "file_sha256" "6884fe35829bc5bfacf0148ddddb8ee441b842cbc9f885bcf5b9b0c932c1d8c8"} {"question" "q-326300" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that a curve is defined parametrically as\n\n$$\nx=3-\\frac{1}{2}t,\\,y=\\frac{3}{4}{t}^{2}-1,\\,t\\ge 2.\n$$\n\nDetermine the ranges of $x$ and $y.$\n\n$x$\n{{field-1}}{{field-2}}$,\\,y$\n{{field-3}}{{field-4}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033872/state.json" "file_sha256" "6884fe35829bc5bfacf0148ddddb8ee441b842cbc9f885bcf5b9b0c932c1d8c8"} {"question" "q-326300" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's consider each variable in turn.\n\n- To find the range of $x,$ note that $3-\\frac{1}{2}t\\le 2$ for all $t\\ge 2.$ Consequently, the range of $x$ is\n\n$$\nx\\le 2.\n$$\n\n- To find the range of $y,$ note that $\\frac{3}{4}{t}^{2}-1\\ge 2$ for all $t\\ge 2.$ Consequently, the range of $y$ is\n\n$$\ny\\ge 2.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033872/state.json" "file_sha256" "6884fe35829bc5bfacf0148ddddb8ee441b842cbc9f885bcf5b9b0c932c1d8c8"} {"question" "q-326300" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033872/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b47cbfa9e32ceac06bca1e70e5aba7e83a133b3e6bc5cebf3ecfee8b04c7ad85"} {"question" "q-326300" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033872/state.json" "file_sha256" "6884fe35829bc5bfacf0148ddddb8ee441b842cbc9f885bcf5b9b0c932c1d8c8"} {"question" "q-326300" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\le"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033872/state.json" "file_sha256" "6884fe35829bc5bfacf0148ddddb8ee441b842cbc9f885bcf5b9b0c932c1d8c8"} {"question" "q-326300" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033872/state.json" "file_sha256" "6884fe35829bc5bfacf0148ddddb8ee441b842cbc9f885bcf5b9b0c932c1d8c8"} {"question" "q-326300" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033872/state.json" "file_sha256" "6884fe35829bc5bfacf0148ddddb8ee441b842cbc9f885bcf5b9b0c932c1d8c8"} {"question" "q-326300" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033872/state.json" "file_sha256" "6884fe35829bc5bfacf0148ddddb8ee441b842cbc9f885bcf5b9b0c932c1d8c8"} {"question" "q-326300" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\ge"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033872/state.json" "file_sha256" "6884fe35829bc5bfacf0148ddddb8ee441b842cbc9f885bcf5b9b0c932c1d8c8"} {"question" "q-326300" "field" "field-4" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033872/state.json" "file_sha256" "6884fe35829bc5bfacf0148ddddb8ee441b842cbc9f885bcf5b9b0c932c1d8c8"} {"question" "q-326300" "field" "field-4" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033872/state.json" "file_sha256" "6884fe35829bc5bfacf0148ddddb8ee441b842cbc9f885bcf5b9b0c932c1d8c8"} {"question" "q-275807" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A point $P$ has Cartesian coordinates $(-1,-1).$ Find the polar coordinates of $P.$ Give the polar angle in radians and do not round the answer.\n\nThe polar coordinates of $P$ are $(${{field-1}}$,$\n{{field-2}}$).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033872/state.json" "file_sha256" "6884fe35829bc5bfacf0148ddddb8ee441b842cbc9f885bcf5b9b0c932c1d8c8"} {"question" "q-275807" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we determine $r:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-1)^{2}+(-1)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1+1} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor the reference angle, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\theta }_{R} & =|\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{y}{x})| \\\\  & =|\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{-1}{-1})| \\\\  & =|\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(1)| \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the point $P$ lies in the third quadrant, we add the reference angle to $\\pi ,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\theta  & =\\pi +{\\theta }_{R} \\\\  & =\\pi +\\frac{\\pi }{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{5\\pi }{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the polar coordinates of $P$ are  $(\\sqrt{2},\\frac{5\\pi }{4}).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033872/state.json" "file_sha256" "6884fe35829bc5bfacf0148ddddb8ee441b842cbc9f885bcf5b9b0c932c1d8c8"} {"question" "q-275807" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033872/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b47cbfa9e32ceac06bca1e70e5aba7e83a133b3e6bc5cebf3ecfee8b04c7ad85"} {"question" "q-275807" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033872/state.json" "file_sha256" "6884fe35829bc5bfacf0148ddddb8ee441b842cbc9f885bcf5b9b0c932c1d8c8"} {"question" "q-275807" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\sqrt{2}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033872/state.json" "file_sha256" "6884fe35829bc5bfacf0148ddddb8ee441b842cbc9f885bcf5b9b0c932c1d8c8"} {"question" "q-275807" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033872/state.json" "file_sha256" "6884fe35829bc5bfacf0148ddddb8ee441b842cbc9f885bcf5b9b0c932c1d8c8"} {"question" "q-275807" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{5\\pi}{4}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033872/state.json" "file_sha256" "6884fe35829bc5bfacf0148ddddb8ee441b842cbc9f885bcf5b9b0c932c1d8c8"} {"question" "q-51143" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that \n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}+31}{(x-2)^{2}(2x+1)}=\\frac{A}{x-2}+\\frac{B}{(x-2)^{2}}+\\frac{C}{2x+1},\n$$\n\nwhere $A$, $B$, and $C$ are real constants, determine the value of $A\\cdot B\\cdot C.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033872/state.json" "file_sha256" "6884fe35829bc5bfacf0148ddddb8ee441b842cbc9f885bcf5b9b0c932c1d8c8"} {"question" "q-51143" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Multiplying both sides of the given equality by $(x-2)^{2}(2x+1)$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+31 & =A(x-2)(2x+1)+B(2x+1)+C(x-2)^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLetting $x=-\\frac{1}{2}$  gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(-\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}+31 & =A(-\\frac{1}{2}-2)(2[-\\frac{1}{2}]+1)+B(2[-\\frac{1}{2}]+1)+C{(-\\frac{1}{2}-2)}^{2} \\\\ \\frac{1}{4}+31 & =A(-\\frac{5}{2})(-1+1)+B(-1+1)+C(\\frac{25}{4}) \\\\ \\frac{125}{4} & =\\frac{25C}{4} \\\\ C & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLetting $x=2$  gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{2}^{2}+31 & =A(2-2)(2\\cdot 2+1)+B(2\\cdot 2+1)+C(2-2)^{2} \\\\ 35 & =5B \\\\ B & =7.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, letting $x=0$ and using our values for $B$ and $C$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{0}^{2}+31 & =A(0-2)(2\\cdot 0+1)+7(2\\cdot 0+1)+5(0-2)^{2} \\\\ 31 & =-2A+7+20 \\\\ 31 & =-2A+27 \\\\ 2A & =-4 \\\\ A & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nHence,\n\n$$\nA\\cdot B\\cdot C=(-2)\\cdot 7\\cdot 5=-70.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033872/state.json" "file_sha256" "6884fe35829bc5bfacf0148ddddb8ee441b842cbc9f885bcf5b9b0c932c1d8c8"} {"question" "q-51143" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033872/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b47cbfa9e32ceac06bca1e70e5aba7e83a133b3e6bc5cebf3ecfee8b04c7ad85"} {"question" "q-51143" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033872/state.json" "file_sha256" "6884fe35829bc5bfacf0148ddddb8ee441b842cbc9f885bcf5b9b0c932c1d8c8"} {"question" "q-51143" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-42"] ["math" "-56"] ["math" "-70"] ["math" "50"] ["math" "64"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033872/state.json" "file_sha256" "6884fe35829bc5bfacf0148ddddb8ee441b842cbc9f885bcf5b9b0c932c1d8c8"} {"question" "q-51143" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-70"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033872/state.json" "file_sha256" "6884fe35829bc5bfacf0148ddddb8ee441b842cbc9f885bcf5b9b0c932c1d8c8"} {"question" "q-42432" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The minimum value of $y=\\operatorname{arccos}⁡x$ is" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033872/state.json" "file_sha256" "6884fe35829bc5bfacf0148ddddb8ee441b842cbc9f885bcf5b9b0c932c1d8c8"} {"question" "q-42432" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's recall the graph of $y=\\operatorname{arccos}⁡x.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033872/assets/d2677563c82c37fd1672a806a18524c97ea5ec17cb4f8ef6d8df23b827ba5e81.png)\n\nFrom the graph, we see that the minimum value is $0.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033872/state.json" "file_sha256" "6884fe35829bc5bfacf0148ddddb8ee441b842cbc9f885bcf5b9b0c932c1d8c8"} {"question" "q-42432" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033872/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b47cbfa9e32ceac06bca1e70e5aba7e83a133b3e6bc5cebf3ecfee8b04c7ad85"} {"question" "q-42432" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033872/state.json" "file_sha256" "6884fe35829bc5bfacf0148ddddb8ee441b842cbc9f885bcf5b9b0c932c1d8c8"} {"question" "q-42432" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-2\\pi "] ["math" "-\\frac{3\\pi }{2}"] ["math" "-\\frac{5\\pi }{2}"] ["math" "-\\pi "] ["math" "0"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033872/state.json" "file_sha256" "6884fe35829bc5bfacf0148ddddb8ee441b842cbc9f885bcf5b9b0c932c1d8c8"} {"question" "q-42432" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "0"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033872/state.json" "file_sha256" "6884fe35829bc5bfacf0148ddddb8ee441b842cbc9f885bcf5b9b0c932c1d8c8"} {"question" "q-72450" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate $\\int (\\frac{1}{5x+2}+\\frac{1}{5x-2})\\,\\text{d}x.$ Assume that $K$ is an arbitrary positive constant." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033872/state.json" "file_sha256" "6884fe35829bc5bfacf0148ddddb8ee441b842cbc9f885bcf5b9b0c932c1d8c8"} {"question" "q-72450" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's solve this using the general formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (\\frac{1}{5x+2}+\\frac{1}{5x-2})\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{5x+2}\\,\\text{d}x+\\int \\frac{1}{5x-2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|5x+2|+\\frac{1}{5}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|5x-2|+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|(5x+2)(5x-2)|+\\frac{1}{5}\\operatorname{ln}⁡K \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(K|(5x+2)(5x-2)|)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that we used the laws of logarithms to write the result as a single logarithm." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033872/state.json" "file_sha256" "6884fe35829bc5bfacf0148ddddb8ee441b842cbc9f885bcf5b9b0c932c1d8c8"} {"question" "q-72450" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033872/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b47cbfa9e32ceac06bca1e70e5aba7e83a133b3e6bc5cebf3ecfee8b04c7ad85"} {"question" "q-72450" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033872/state.json" "file_sha256" "6884fe35829bc5bfacf0148ddddb8ee441b842cbc9f885bcf5b9b0c932c1d8c8"} {"question" "q-72450" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "5\\operatorname{ln}⁡(K|(5x+2)(5x-2)|)"] ["math" "5\\operatorname{ln}⁡(K|\\frac{5x+2}{5x-2}|)"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{5}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(K|(5x+2)(5x-2)|)"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{5}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(K|\\frac{5x+2}{5x-2}|)"] ["math" "\\operatorname{ln}⁡(K|\\frac{5x+2}{5x-2}|)"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033872/state.json" "file_sha256" "6884fe35829bc5bfacf0148ddddb8ee441b842cbc9f885bcf5b9b0c932c1d8c8"} {"question" "q-72450" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{5}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(K|(5x+2)(5x-2)|)"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033872/state.json" "file_sha256" "68